1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,820
At 9:12 Monday, an $84,600 invoice
enters the agent's queue.

2
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:11,940
Mismatch: 6.2%. Supplier warning:
shipments may stop in 48 hours.

3
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:17,740
The rulebook has one sentence: resolve material
discrepancies with the appropriate approver.

4
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:22,360
Then the cast arrives. Accounts Payable:
"Hold it. Records do not match."

5
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:27,860
Procurement: "Release it. Protect supply."
Operations: "Pay it. Correct it later."

6
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:31,420
Three reasonable answers.
Together, no decision.

7
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:35,000
The reveal: the agent is not confused.
The organization has never made five things explicit:

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,440
Outcome. Owner. Decision right.
Exception path. Success measure.

9
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:44,600
Humans bridge gaps through memory
and hallway conversations.

10
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,600
Agents cannot safely inherit rules
that were never written down.

11
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:53,080
Before adding an agent, give the same exception
to two experienced people.

12
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:57,840
If they cannot explain the decision the same way,
you do not have an agent problem.

13
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:59,920
You have an organization-design problem.
